      "description": "The SKY Brasil - Jaguariúna facility, located at Rod. SP-340 Km133 in Jaguariúna, Brazil, is a cutting-edge broadcast center and data center. It was designed to meet SKY's channel and service demands for the next 15 years, prioritizing reliability, availability, sustainability, and operational flexibility.\n\nThe facility is a Tier 3 data center, recognized with the Data Center Dynamics award in 2015. It features a 2N+1 configuration for its own power generation, exceeding Tier 4 standards. The infrastructure includes redundant systems for air conditioning, fire suppression, power supply and generation, signal reception and transmission, and access control, ensuring 24/7 operation.\n\nWith 17,000 m² of built area on a 33,000 m² plot, the center supports up to 700 employees. Its design incorporates advanced technologies for energy efficiency, such as internal transmitters in antennas and a heat exchange system for air conditioning that saves significant amounts of water. The project represents a substantial investment, aiming to triple SKY's capacity and serve as a redundant operation to its existing data center.",
